<p>Gutters rarely get attention until they overflow in a thunderstorm or pull loose from the fascia. Yet in Central Texas, where a single storm can dump heavy rain in a short time, the drainage system at the roof edge does a lot of quiet work. Temple Roofers installs and repairs <strong>gutters in Temple, TX</strong>, along with downspouts, drip edge and related roof-edge components. We look at the whole path water takes, from the shingles to the ground, and make sure each piece is sized and pitched to handle it.</p>

<h2>Warning Signs of Drainage Problems</h2>
<p>Most gutter trouble is visible from the ground, especially during or just after a rain. Watch for:</p>
<ul>
<li>Water spilling over the front or back of gutters during heavy rain</li>
<li>Gutters sagging, leaning outward or separating from the fascia</li>
