<tr><td>Downspouts</td><td>2x3-inch or 3x4-inch</td><td>Larger downspouts and more of them reduce overflow; spacing and placement matter as much as size</td></tr>
<tr><td>Extensions and outlets</td><td>Splash blocks, extensions, underground drain lines</td><td>Discharge water away from the foundation and toward areas that drain well</td></tr>
<tr><td>Gutter guards</td><td>Screens, micro-mesh, surface-tension covers</td><td>Reduce clogging from leaves and debris; none are maintenance-free and some can shed water in very heavy rain</td></tr>
